This leads to the following research question:
\begin{center}
{\em Which connected graphs are almost classified?}
\end{center}

\label{t-schindl}
For $p\geq 1$, let $H_1,\ldots,H_p$ be graphs whose complement is not in~${\cal T}$.
Then {\sc Colouring} is {\sf NP}-complete for $(H_1,\ldots,H_p)$-free graphs.
